course: dictionary
lesson: 10895
title: Virgo: a name in the sky
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Virgo» starts with a capital letter, so it is a proper noun: the name of one special thing, not a general word. Read the clues around it. «In spring, follow the curve of the Plough's handle to "arc to Arcturus" and then "speed on to Spica" in Virgo.» Words like follow, curve and speed on tell you that Virgo is a place you find by looking up at the night sky.
explain: The words «Spica» and «in Virgo» tell you that Virgo is a group of stars, and Spica is one bright star inside it. A group of stars that people have named is called a constellation. The dictionary says Virgo's name is Latin for «the virgin» or «young woman».
explain: Virgo has a second meaning, too. In magazines, Virgo is one of the twelve star signs of the zodiac, for people born from about 23 August to 22 September, and a person with that sign is also called a Virgo. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: «in Virgo» still makes sense when you think of the sky, so the sky meaning is the right one here.
fact: «Virgo» is a proper noun because it is the name of one particular constellation and sign.
fact: A constellation is a group of stars that people have named and pictured as a shape.
fact: «Spica» is a bright star in Virgo.
fact: The name Virgo comes from Latin and means «the virgin» or «young woman».
fact: Astronomy is the science of stars and space; astrology, which uses star signs to try to tell your future, is not science.
exercise: «In spring, follow the curve of the Plough's handle to "arc to Arcturus" and then "speed on to Spica" in Virgo.» In this sentence, what is Virgo? | A bright planet that moves across the sky | A magazine about spring | *A group of stars in the sky | A kind of cloud near the Plough
exercise: Virgo's name is Latin for what? | The Plough's handle | *The virgin or young woman | A twelve-pointed shape | A bright star
exercise: A magazine says, «Virgo, you will meet a new friend this week.» Which meaning of Virgo is used here? | *A person born under the star sign Virgo, roughly 23 August to 22 September | A group of hills in the north | A constellation with the bright star Spica | Latin for a long journey
test: What is the bright star in Virgo named in the sentence? | Arcturus | Virgo | The Plough | *Spica
test: Which subject studies stars and space as science? | Astrology | Magazines about spring | Horoscopes | *Astronomy
exam: Which statement about Virgo is correct? | Virgo is the name of a bright star only, and nothing else | Virgo is a common noun, so it starts with a small letter | Virgo means the Plough's handle in Latin | *Virgo is a constellation, a star sign, and can also mean a person born under that sign
